{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8f879536012842e8ddc896470e33cfa63fca6e6aa9baaef0d4065f2f38e176c7","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar CLI argument parsing","key_entities":["rebar comment","rebar create","rebar edit","rebar session-log","rebar tag","rebar untag","rebar archive","rebar set-verify-commands","--body-file","--body","args[:min_args]"],"problem_keywords":["cli parsing","silent data loss","positional argument","flag token","durability","exit code 0"],"propositions":["rebar comment accepts flag-looking tokens (--body-file, --body) as the body argument and stores the flag string itself instead of the intended content","the command exits with code 0 and produces no error output when a flag token is mistakenly passed as body, making the loss undetectable until content is read","positional-body commands (comment, create, edit, session-log, tag, untag, archive, set-verify-commands) lack validation to reject arguments beginning with dash, allowing silent overwrites of intended content","the -- escape hatch must be implemented and documented to permit legitimate body values that begin with a dash","a test suite must verify rejection of --body-file and --body flag forms across the affected commands"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787648947840626713,"uuid":"cc273ba2-82cf-4bfa-838b-feff2f6b8e07"}